    meaning: "The 'fen' in Chunfen has a double meaning: first, day and night divide evenly — the sun stands directly over the equator and nearly everywhere on earth has almost equal day and night; second, it divides spring in half, being the midpoint between Lichun and Lixia, hence the alternate names 'Sun at the Center' and 'Division of Day and Night'. Chunfen falls when the sun reaches celestial longitude 0° (the vernal equinox point), usually between March 20 and 22, and is the fourth solar term of spring. The vernal equinox point is also the zero point from which ecliptic coordinates are measured in astronomy. Afterward the sun's direct rays move northward, and in the northern hemisphere days grow longer and nights shorter.",
